      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1880s, the California Southern Railroad was constructed through the valley to connect National City and San Bernardino with Chinese laborers who previously worked on the Central Pacific Railroad in the 1860s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
